WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.046
Lecture sixteen defined the determinant

2
00:00:06.126 --> 00:00:07.336
by three rules

3
00:00:07.336 --> 00:00:09.756
and drew it as a signed area.

4
00:00:09.756 --> 00:00:12.740
Today, the formula behind the rules.

5
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.809
Take the rows four, one and one, two.

6
00:00:16.809 --> 00:00:20.930
They span a parallelogram of area seven.

7
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.914
Rule three lets us split a row into pieces.

8
00:00:25.914 --> 00:00:30.225
Four, one is four, zero plus zero, one.

9
00:00:30.225 --> 00:00:34.320
One, two is one, zero plus zero, two.

10
00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.036
Splitting both rows gives four pieces.

11
00:00:38.036 --> 00:00:40.604
Which of them keep any area?

12
00:00:40.604 --> 00:00:42.110
Pause and think.

13
00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:49.170
Two pieces use the same direction twice

14
00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.215
four, zero with one, zero is flat

15
00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:55.347
and so is zero, one with zero, two.

16
00:00:55.347 --> 00:00:56.130
No area.

17
00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.898
Four, zero with zero, two is a rectangle

18
00:01:00.898 --> 00:01:04.022
plus eight, the product a d.

19
00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:08.763
Zero, one with one, zero is a small square

20
00:01:08.763 --> 00:01:11.349
but it turns clockwise

21
00:01:11.349 --> 00:01:15.120
so it counts minus one: minus b c.

22
00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:19.720
Eight minus one is seven: a d minus b c

23
00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.270
rebuilt from the rules.

24
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.534
For any size the same thing happens.

25
00:01:25.615 --> 00:01:28.610
A piece survives only if it takes one

26
00:01:28.691 --> 00:01:31.606
entry from each row and each column

27
00:01:31.606 --> 00:01:32.820
a permutation.

28
00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.220
Its sign is the sign of that permutation.

29
00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:40.053
For two by two, the two surviving pieces are

30
00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:41.794
the two permutations

31
00:01:41.794 --> 00:01:44.644
the rectangle and the small square.

32
00:01:44.723 --> 00:01:46.623
For three by three there

33
00:01:46.702 --> 00:01:49.551
would be six pieces, and for n by n

34
00:01:49.551 --> 00:01:52.955
one for each of the n factorial orderings.

35
00:01:52.955 --> 00:01:54.697
That grows very fast.

36
00:01:54.776 --> 00:01:56.992
Elimination needs only about

37
00:01:57.071 --> 00:01:59.050
n cubed over three steps.

38
00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.075
Now group the terms by the

39
00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:05.725
entries of row one.

40
00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:09.435
a d minus b c is a times d

41
00:02:09.435 --> 00:02:12.350
plus b times minus c.

42
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:16.059
The multipliers d and minus c are

43
00:02:16.161 --> 00:02:18.706
the cofactors of row one.

44
00:02:18.706 --> 00:02:21.658
As a vector, two, minus one

45
00:02:21.759 --> 00:02:24.610
it is row two turned a right

46
00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.340
angle clockwise.

47
00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:30.133
So the determinant is a dot product

48
00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:33.959
row one dotted with n, eight minus one

49
00:02:33.959 --> 00:02:34.629
seven.

50
00:02:34.629 --> 00:02:38.837
Geometrically, the length of n is the base

51
00:02:38.933 --> 00:02:42.854
and the dot product measures how high row

52
00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:46.393
one rises above the line of row two.

53
00:02:46.393 --> 00:02:48.210
Base times height.

54
00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.833
The same holds in every size

55
00:02:50.912 --> 00:02:54.047
the cofactors of a row are perpendicular

56
00:02:54.125 --> 00:02:55.850
to all the other rows

57
00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.907
so they always give base times height.

58
00:02:58.907 --> 00:03:02.042
Each cofactor is a smaller determinant

59
00:03:02.042 --> 00:03:04.080
with a checkerboard sign.

60
00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.991
Expand along row two instead.

61
00:03:06.991 --> 00:03:10.348
Its cofactors are minus one and four

62
00:03:10.436 --> 00:03:14.499
row one turned a right angle counterclockwise.

63
00:03:14.587 --> 00:03:17.060
One times minus one plus two

64
00:03:17.148 --> 00:03:19.445
times four is seven again.

65
00:03:19.445 --> 00:03:21.653
A zero entry saves work

66
00:03:21.653 --> 00:03:24.037
if row two were zero, two

67
00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:28.012
only one term would survive, two times four

68
00:03:28.012 --> 00:03:28.630
eight.

69
00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:30.295
A common slip

70
00:03:30.295 --> 00:03:33.783
all four entries of our matrix are positive

71
00:03:33.783 --> 00:03:36.650
so both pieces must get a plus sign?

72
00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.230
That gives nine, not seven.

73
00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.488
It counts the clockwise square as positive

74
00:03:42.563 --> 00:03:44.858
and eight plus one is more than

75
00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:46.710
the whole parallelogram.

76
00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.436
The minus sign belongs to the position

77
00:03:49.436 --> 00:03:50.533
not to the entry.

78
00:03:50.594 --> 00:03:52.300
Keep the checkerboard in the

79
00:03:52.361 --> 00:03:53.580
corner of your page.

80
00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.892
Cofactors also give the inverse.

81
00:03:56.892 --> 00:04:00.648
The cofactors of row one, the vector n one

82
00:04:00.648 --> 00:04:03.209
are perpendicular to row two.

83
00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.879
The cofactors of row two, minus one, four

84
00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.440
are perpendicular to row one.

85
00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:14.545
So row one times n one is the determinant

86
00:04:14.545 --> 00:04:18.281
and row two times n one is zero.

87
00:04:18.281 --> 00:04:22.243
Put the cofactors into a matrix C

88
00:04:22.356 --> 00:04:25.526
A times C transpose is seven

89
00:04:25.639 --> 00:04:27.790
times the identity.

90
00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.309
The inverse is C transpose

91
00:04:30.392 --> 00:04:32.144
over the determinant.

92
00:04:32.144 --> 00:04:33.813
Note the transpose.

93
00:04:33.813 --> 00:04:36.732
For two by two it is the old rule

94
00:04:36.732 --> 00:04:40.153
swap the diagonal, negate the other two

95
00:04:40.153 --> 00:04:40.820
divide.

96
00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.287
Last, Cramer's rule

97
00:04:43.287 --> 00:04:46.118
which works with the columns.

98
00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:49.892
Take the columns two, one and one, two

99
00:04:49.892 --> 00:04:51.024
area three.

100
00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:54.326
We want b, four, three and a half

101
00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:57.440
as x one a one plus x two a two.

102
00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.399
Replace column one by b.

103
00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:05.292
Keep a faint copy, then slide b along a two

104
00:05:05.292 --> 00:05:08.771
sliding never changes the area

105
00:05:08.771 --> 00:05:12.794
and b lands on one and a half a one.

106
00:05:12.903 --> 00:05:15.838
So the area of b with a two

107
00:05:15.947 --> 00:05:18.230
is x one times three.

108
00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.413
That is Cramer's rule

109
00:05:20.413 --> 00:05:23.495
x one is four and a half over three

110
00:05:23.495 --> 00:05:24.828
one and a half.

111
00:05:24.911 --> 00:05:27.327
Replacing column two the same

112
00:05:27.411 --> 00:05:29.660
way gives x two equals one.

113
00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:30.550
Check

114
00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:34.238
one and a half a one plus a two is four

115
00:05:34.238 --> 00:05:36.936
three and a half, which is b.

116
00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:40.714
But Cramer needs n plus one determinants.

117
00:05:40.714 --> 00:05:44.132
Use it for two by two and for proofs.

118
00:05:44.132 --> 00:05:47.010
Solve numbers with elimination.

119
00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:50.198
So: the big formula has one

120
00:05:50.294 --> 00:05:52.323
term per permutation.

121
00:05:52.323 --> 00:05:55.317
Cofactors organise it by rows

122
00:05:55.317 --> 00:05:59.470
and point perpendicular to the other rows.

123
00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:03.191
That perpendicularity gives the inverse

124
00:06:03.191 --> 00:06:06.056
C transpose over the determinant

125
00:06:06.056 --> 00:06:07.658
and Cramer's rule

126
00:06:07.658 --> 00:06:10.860
by sliding b along the other columns.

127
00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:15.152
In part two: what the determinant measures.

128
00:06:15.152 --> 00:06:16.792
An area, a volume

129
00:06:16.879 --> 00:06:19.641
and the factor by which a matrix

130
00:06:19.728 --> 00:06:21.454
scales every region

131
00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.476
which machine learning uses inside

132
00:06:24.562 --> 00:06:26.720
its probability formulas.
